 "summary": {
  "version": 2,
  "basis": "em",
  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2022-07-27",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would change tax treatment for cyclone recovery grants and the Women’s World Cup, manage superannuation complaint transitions and make technical legislative amendments.",
   "It would exclude qualifying Cyclone Seroja grants from taxable income and provide limited tournament-related tax exemptions, while supporting the transfer of former tribunal responsibilities.",
   "Separate technical measures would delay the automatic commencement of business register modernisation legislation until 1 July 2026, unless an earlier date was proclaimed."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The cyclone grant tax treatment would apply from the 2021-2022 income year.",
   "Former Superannuation Complaints Tribunal records would become the Australian Securities and Investments Commission’s responsibility, with confidentiality protections.",
   "The Federal Court could send former tribunal matters to the Australian Financial Complaints Authority for redetermination.",
   "The International Federation of Association Football and FWWC2023 Pty Ltd would receive relevant tournament tax exemptions covering 1 July 2020 to 31 December 2028."
  ],
  "affected": "Eligible cyclone-affected businesses and primary producers, superannuation complainants, tournament organisers and entities using business registers would be affected.",
